e>Norman</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>Health Measurement Scales: A practical guide to their development and use</source><edition>2nd ed</edition><publisher-loc>Oxford, UK</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name><year>2000</year></element-citation></ref><ref id="b16-dhps-1-009"><label>16.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cronin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Guyatt</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffith</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Development of a health&#x02013;related quality-of-life questionnaire (PCOSQ) for women with polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS)</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>1998</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1976</fpage><lpage>1987</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9626128</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b17-dhps-1-009"><label>17.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eggers</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirchengast</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The polycystic ovary syndrome &#x02013; a medical condition but also an important psychosocial problem</article-title><source>Coll Antropol</source><year>2001</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>673</fpage><lpage>685</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11811299</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b18-dhps-1-009"><label>18.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirchengast</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vytiska-Binstorfer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Huber</surname><given-names>J</given-names></